SUMMARY:STUDY · Maths — Continuity · limits & first piecewise checks
DESCRIPTION:Phase 1 · Day 1/10 · 105 min · IST\n\n1. Recall · 10 min\nR
 ecall yesterday’s method. If basic algebra or limits block the first que
 stion\, use the bridge guide for these 10 minutes.\n\n2. Learn · 40 min\n
 Confirm the bridge check from 24–25 Oct\, then NCERT 5.2 (PDF pp. 1–13
 ): LHL\, RHL and f(a). Use the continuity video only for this topic\; take
  a 5-minute pause.\nVideo · matching topic only:\nhttps://www.youtube.com
 /watch?v=paNnEHzOfJw\nNCERT · PDF p. 13:\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/p
 df/lemh105.pdf#page=13\n\n3. Practise · 40 min\nEx. 5.1 Q1\, Q3 (all part
 s)\, Q6 and Q12. Show both one-sided limits at each joining point.\nNCERT 
 questions · PDF p. 13:\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/lemh105.pdf#pag
 e=13\nMaths prerequisite guide: Resources/phase-01/maths-precalculus-bridg
 e.html\n\n4. Check & record · 15 min\nCheck the answers and working. Reat
 tempt the first wrong item\; record any unfinished question number.\nNCERT
  final answers: Sources/Books/maths-part-1/lemh1an.pdf\n\nUnfinished? Save
  the exact question\; repair it at the next same-subject start. Saved file
 s open from the project folder through planner.html.
